# Fixed-width subtype store normalizes a promoted value

Verifies an `int8<mm>[]` store accepts a millimeter value that was evaluated
with a wider temporary representation. `2mm + 127mm` overflows `int8`, and
subtracting `127mm` again yields `2mm`, which fits `int8` and stays the
declared millimeter subtype.

>>> source
let a: int8<mm>[] = [2mm]
a[0] = (a[0] + 127mm) - 127mm
print(a[0])

<<< stdout
2mm

<<< stderr
